     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Thats how I create my first reactiveValues()<br></div><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">myDataSet </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reactiveValues</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NULL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>I have an &quot;actionButton&quot;. When that is clicked this line is executed:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">observeEvent</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$go</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{<br></span><span style=\"color:#000\">myDataSet$data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> go</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span></div></code></div><br>&quot;go-df&quot; is a dataframe with a few NA`s spread in the rows (but not many)!<br><br>I wait for further input from the &quot;ui.R&quot; for subsetting. I store the subsetted results again in `reactiveValues`.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">d</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ataSetAbsolute </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reactiveValues</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">test1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NULL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> test2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NULL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>observe</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>dataSetAbsolute$test1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> subset</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> myDataSet$data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>subset </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> myDataSet$data$columnx </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> input$chosenbyuser<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> na</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">omit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(.))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span></div></code></div><br>That seems  to work right. To check I do &quot;str(dataSetAbsolute $test1)&quot; to see whats in there and what I get is rather confusing.<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;data.frame&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> obs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> of  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">22</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> variables</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span></div></code></div><br>It lists everything and everything is empty exept for three columns. <b>Then</b>, this is followed by <br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;data.frame&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> obs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> of  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">22</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> variables</span></div></code></div><br>There, everything is filled how it is supposed to be. <br><br>How can I understand that?!<br>Why are there two dataframes behind &quot;dataSetAbsolute$test1&quot;?<br>Do I missunderstand how &quot;reactiveValues()&quot; work and what they are there for?!</div>"
    ]
